            {
              "id": "3d5863fd-1652-3cf1-aefe-308fabd190b1",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe \"Prohibited C Function Found\" vulnerability refers to the use of certain C library functions that are considered unsafe due to their potential to cause buffer overflows, format string vulnerabilities, or other security issues. In this case, the function `freopen()` is used, which can lead to potential security risks if not used properly.\n\nThe `freopen()` function is used to close the current file associated with the given stream and reassign the stream to another file. If the filename is NULL, the stream is reassigned to the default file (stdin, stdout, or stderr). This can lead to potential security issues if the filename is controlled by an attacker.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to avoid using the `freopen()` function if possible. Instead, use safer alternatives that do not have the same potential for security issues. For example, you can use the `fopen()` function to open a file and the `fclose()` function to close it. \n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nHere is a safer alternative to the `freopen()` function:\n\n```cpp\nFILE* file = fopen(logFilename.c_str(), \"w\");\nif (file != NULL) {\n    fclose(stdout);\n    stdout = file;\n}\n```\n\nThis code opens the file using `fopen()` and then closes `stdout` using `fclose()`. It then assigns the file to `stdout`. This avoids the potential security issues associated with `freopen()`.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the following library dependencies:\n\n- `<cstdio>`: This library is required for the `freopen()`, `fopen()`, and `fclose()` functions.\n\n## OWASP and CWE Links\n\n- [OWASP C++](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Buffer_overflow_attack)\n- [CWE-676: Use of Potentially Dangerous Function](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/676.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "DS154189"
                ]
              }
